# x4_stream_load: checkpoint streamed tensor by tensor; the whole model is never built. Row five of the
# per-layer arm.
#
# object     p_census_peak_x2 (97.5%): 866.5 MB float32 weights in pairs (state_dict and module).
#            after_model_load 1,150,172 kB; 0.5 s later 384,688.
# before     x3 (low_cpu_mem_usage=True): after_model_load 1,150,172 -> 300,084, run worse (1,506,944 vs
#            1,139,484; peak moved 4.5 s later into conversion).
# lever      safe_open (tensor-wise mmap) per scope; twelve encoder layers to disk as state_dicts;
#            posix_fadvise(DONTNEED) on faulted pages.
# donor      retired s6_stream_load:
#              s3_disk        1,295,888 kB
#              s4_reduce      1,333,064      a REGRESSION there, contrary to its own summary.md
#              s5_embed_chunk   962,480
#              s6_stream_load   643,784      = 628.7 MiB, the "629 MiB" this repo cites
#            departure: its per-scope shards (split_safetensors.py, outside the measured process)
#            dropped; model.safetensors read directly, fadvise after each scope.
# free       same weights, file and order; three sub-models under torch.random.fork_rng().
# gate       identical to x2's expected.
# expected   1,135,384 kB -> 700 to 850 MB (-25% to -40%); x2 spread 11%.
SHAFT_SCRIPT=$BASE/bert_perlayer_stream_cpu.py
SHAFT_LEVERS=plaintext_free_cpu,triple_share_free_cpu,trace_nograd_cpu,onnx_single_file_export_cpu,encrypt_spill_cpu,embed_chunk_cpu
SHAFT_INNER_ENV="SHAFT_EMBED_CHUNKS=16"
